## Problem: Accepted Candidates From the Interview

A company is looking for experienced candidates. An interview process consists of two rounds. A candidate is considered accepted if their score is greater than 15 in both rounds.
Write a solution to find the IDs of all candidates who are accepted.

Table Schemas & Data:

Candidates table:
| candidate_id | name |
| --- | --- |
| 101 | Kael |
| 102 | Mirana |
| 103 | Puck |
| 104 | Lina |

Rounds table:
| interview_id | candidate_id | round_number | score |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 101 | 1 | 18 |
| 2 | 101 | 2 | 25 |
| 3 | 102 | 1 | 19 |
| 4 | 102 | 2 | 12 |
| 5 | 103 | 1 | 20 |
| 6 | 104 | 1 | 8 |
| 7 | 104 | 2 | 9 |

Expected Output:
[101]

Solution : 
import pandas as pd
def accepted_candidates(candidates: pd.DataFrame, rounds: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:
    passed_rounds = Rounds[Rounds['score'] > 15]
    candidate_counts = passed_rounds.groupby('candidate_id').size()
    accepted_candidates = candidate_counts[candidate_counts['candidate_counts'] == 2]
    return accepted_candidates
